{"Title":"An Act relative to state employment postings","BillNumber":"S1150","DocketNumber":"SD272","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"JMC0","Name":"Joanne M. Comerford","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JMC0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-12T11:53:56.163"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"JMC0","Name":"Joanne M. Comerford","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JMC0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-12T11:53:56.1633333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1150/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Ms. Comerford, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1150) of Joanne M. Comerford for legislation relative to state employment postings.  Labor and Workforce Development.","DocumentText":"\tSection 4J of chapter 7 of the General Laws is hereby amended by adding the following paragraph:-\r\n\tEvery agency and institution of the commonwealth shall transmit to the human resources division all employment opportunities, notices, and postings, excluding positions subject to section 46D of chapter 30, chapter 31 and chapter 150E, including, but not limited to, notices of job opportunities, new positions and vacancies. The division shall immediately place all such information in the statewide employment computerized referral system. No position shall be filled without full compliance with this paragraph.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J43","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J43"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}